message: "If you use GuideBPMN, please cite it as below."
title: "GuideBPMN 1.0: An Agentic Tool for BPMN Generation Through Error-Driven Learning"
type: software
version: "1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-19"
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Benmoussa
    given-names: Fatma
    affiliation: "ÉTS, University of Quebec"
  - family-names: Bessghaier
    given-names: Narjes
    affiliation: "ÉTS, University of Quebec"
  - family-names: Benzarti
    given-names: Imen
    affiliation: "ÉTS, University of Quebec"
keywords:
  - BPMN
  - process model generation
  - LLM agents
  - modeling guidelines
abstract: >-
  GuideBPMN generates BPMN 2.0 models from natural-language process descriptions
  with LLMs and learns reusable modeling guidelines from verified errors. It combines
  an LLM-based generator, a four-level structural validator, a reference-based
  similarity evaluator, and guideline agents coordinated by an orchestrator agent.
